<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="avo-ban" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Avocado-Banana Soup</title>

  <p>
    Ingredients
  </p>
  <tabular>
    <row>
      <cell>2 ripe avocados</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>2 medium bananas</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>21 ounces chicken broth</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
    <cell>3 cups half-and-half</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{2}</m> cup dry white vermouth or white wine or grape juice</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{4}</m> cup lime juice</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 tablespoon fresh grated ginger root</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>2 tablespoons sugar</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1/2-1 teaspoon hot pepper sauce (optional)</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>Salt</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>8 ounces shredded crab (optional)</cell>
    </row>
  </tabular>

  <p>Instructions
    <ol>
      <li>
        <p>
          Halve, pit, and peel the avocados.  Puree avocados and bananas with half of the chicken broth in a food processor or blender.  Whip until the mixture is smooth.  Pour into a Dutch oven.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Add half-and-half, vermouth, lime juice, ginger, sugar, hot pepper sauce, salt, and crab.  Stir until well mixed.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Chill or gently heat through, stirring occasionally.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </p>

  <p>
    Notes:
    <ul>
      <li>
        <p>
          
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </p>
</section>